                                    <h1>Skincare D2C Marketing Retainer &amp;mdash; Monthly Structure (2026) | ITD GrowthLabs</h1>
                                    <div style="background:#fef2f2;border-left:4px solid #ec4899;padding:20px 24px;border-radius:10px;margin:24px 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#334155;"><strong style="color:#db2777;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:0.4px;">ITD SKINCARE + BEAUTY PORTFOLIO &mdash; THE EVIDENCE:</strong><br>This article is written from live skincare + beauty vertical work. ITD GrowthLabs is a specialist <a href="/industries/digital-marketing-for-skincare-brands.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">digital marketing agency for skincare brands</a> with 4+ published D2C beauty brand case studies including <a href="/resources/Kama_Ayurveda_Marketing_Strategy_Case_Study_2026.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">Kama Ayurveda</a>, <a href="/resources/Plum_Beauty_Marketing_Strategy_Case_Study_2026.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">Plum Beauty</a>, <a href="/resources/Sugar_Cosmetics_Marketing_Strategy_Case_Study_2026.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">Sugar Cosmetics</a>, and <a href="/resources/WOW_Skin_Science_Marketing_Strategy_Case_Study_2026.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">WOW Skin Science</a>. Plus <a href="/resources/How_Nykaa_Built_India_Largest_Beauty_Brand_2026.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">Nykaa growth story</a>, <a href="/resources/Ayurveda_Traditional_Wellness_D2C_India_Global_2026.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">Ayurveda D2C playbook</a>, seasonal <a href="/resources/Summer_Skincare_Wellness_Playbook_D2C_2026_2027.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">Summer</a> + <a href="/resources/Winter_Skincare_Wellness_Playbook_D2C_2026_2027.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">Winter Skincare</a> playbooks, and 11 GCC city-specific beauty pages (<a href="/services/gcc/dubai-beauty-cosmetics-agency.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">Dubai</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/riyadh-beauty-cosmetics-agency.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">Riyadh</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/jeddah-beauty-cosmetics-agency.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">Jeddah</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/doha-beauty-cosmetics-agency.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">Doha</a>, Abu Dhabi, Dammam, Al Khobar, Kuwait City, Manama, Muscat, Ras al Khaimah). Every framework below is grounded in live category work.</div><p>Marketing retainer = recurring monthly investment in growth engine. Structure matters as much as amount. This piece maps ITD monthly retainer structure: weekly working cadence + monthly QBR + quarterly business review + ad spend transparency + team composition + deliverable volume.</p>
                                    <h2>Weekly working cadence &amp;mdash; all tiers</h2>
                                    <ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li><strong>Monday:</strong> Weekly kickoff + priority + creative + campaign review</li><li><strong>Tuesday-Thursday:</strong> Execution + creative production + ads optimisation + content publish + WhatsApp campaign</li><li><strong>Friday:</strong> Weekly performance snapshot + Slack + email brief + next-week planning</li><li><strong>Ongoing:</strong> Slack + email async communication + response within 4-8 hours business days</li></ul><p>Weekly rhythm keeps velocity + prevents week-of-month lag. Weekly performance snapshot every Friday = single-source-of-truth vs monthly-only reporting.</p>
                                    <h2>Monthly QBR structure</h2>
                                    <ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li>Revenue + AOV + LTV / CAC / cohort recap (30 min)</li><li>Channel-by-channel performance + CPL + ROAS + attribution (30 min)</li><li>Creative + content + campaign highlights + fatigue check (20 min)</li><li>Next month plan + priorities + budget + creative brief (30 min)</li><li>Risks + blockers + strategic decisions (10 min)</li></ul><p>90-120 min monthly. Founder + senior + CMO / head-of-growth attendance. Recorded + shared. Deliverables tracked in shared task board.</p>
                                    <h2>Quarterly business review (QBR)</h2>
                                    <ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li>Quarter recap: revenue + LTV / CAC / cohort trend + subscription retention + repeat rate</li><li>Cohort analysis: month-over-month + quarter-over-quarter + segment-by-segment</li><li>Strategic priorities next quarter: sub-vertical expansion + geographic + channel + retention</li><li>Budget re-planning: retainer + ad spend + creative + creator + PR + tooling</li><li>Team + resource review: scale up / down based on trajectory</li><li>Board-prep materials for VC-backed brands</li></ul><p>Quarterly in-person QBR at Mumbai HQ or client location. Founder + senior + full pod attendance. 3-4 hour session + strategic offsite feel.</p>
                                    <h2>Team composition by tier</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Starter (Rs 65K/mo):</strong> 2-person pod = 1 strategist + 1 execution specialist. Founder + senior on quarterly QBR.</p><p><strong>Growth (Rs 1.8L/mo):</strong> 4-6-person pod = strategist + paid specialist + SEO + content + designer + WhatsApp specialist. Founder + senior monthly.</p><p><strong>Enterprise (Rs 4.5L+/mo):</strong> 5-10-person pod = strategist + paid multi-channel + SEO + content team + creative pod + WhatsApp + creator + PR + regional-language specialists. Founder + senior + CMO partnership continuous.</p><p>Team = named individuals + org chart shared + dedicated (not shared across 10 clients).</p>
                                    <h2>Reporting cadence + deliverables</h2>
                                    <ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li><strong>Weekly:</strong> Friday performance snapshot + Slack brief + next-week priorities</li><li><strong>Bi-weekly:</strong> Creative + content + campaign review + optimisation approvals</li><li><strong>Monthly:</strong> QBR + written performance report + LTV/CAC/cohort update + next-month plan</li><li><strong>Quarterly:</strong> QBR in-person + cohort deep-dive + strategic priorities + budget re-plan + board-prep materials</li><li><strong>Annual:</strong> Year-in-review + next-year strategy + budget planning + team scaling</li></ul><p>Reporting = investor-grade. Numbers + narrative + attribution methodology + assumptions + confidence intervals.</p>
                                    <h2>Ad spend + tooling &amp;mdash; separate line items</h2>
                                    <ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li>Ad spend: transparent pass-through (no markup) &mdash; Rs 40K to Rs 40L+ / month depending on tier</li><li>Photography + video production: bundled into retainer at Mid-market + Enterprise</li><li>Third-party tooling (Klaviyo + Interakt + Judge.me + apps): pass-through or client-billed direct</li><li>Creator + celebrity + PR fees: pass-through with platform receipts or negotiated flat</li><li>Shopify subscription + app fees: client-billed direct</li><li>Legal + trademark + compliance fees: pass-through</li></ul><p>Full transparency = single monthly invoice with retainer line + ad-spend receipts + tooling receipts. No mystery line items. No bundled + markup-inclusive tactic.</p>

                                    <div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 100%); padding: 40px; border-radius: 12px; margin: 40px 0; text-align: center; color: #fff;">
                                        <h3 style="color:#fff;margin-bottom:15px;">Ready to Get Started?</h3>
                                        <p style="color:#ccc;margin-bottom:25px;">Book a free 30-minute skincare D2C discovery call. We map your brand + funnel + share a customised proposal within 3 working days.</p>
